.TH "HTMLTABLEELEMENT.DELETEROW" "3JS" "August 19, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLTableElement.deleteRow \- HTMLTableElement: deleteRow() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]deleteRow()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]HTMLTableElement\f[R] interface removes a specific row
(\f[CR]<tr>\f[R]) from a given \f[CR]<table>\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
deleteRow(index)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]index\f[R]
The index of the row to remove in the \f[CR]rows\f[R] collection.
If \f[CR]index\f[R] is \f[CR]\-1\f[R], the last row is removed.
.SS Return value
None (\f[CR]undefined\f[R]).
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]IndexSizeError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if \f[CR]index\f[R] is greater than or equal to the number of
rows or smaller than \f[CR]\-1\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
This example uses JavaScript to delete a table\(cqs second row.
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]table\f[R]>
  <\f[B]tbody\f[R]>
    <\f[B]tr\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 1.1</\f[B]td\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 1.2</\f[B]td\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 1.3</\f[B]td\f[R]>
    </\f[B]tr\f[R]>
    <\f[B]tr\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 2.1</\f[B]td\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 2.2</\f[B]td\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 2.3</\f[B]td\f[R]>
    </\f[B]tr\f[R]>
    <\f[B]tr\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 3.1</\f[B]td\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 3.2</\f[B]td\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 3.3</\f[B]td\f[R]>
    </\f[B]tr\f[R]>
  </\f[B]tbody\f[R]>
</\f[B]table\f[R]>
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] table = document.querySelector(\(dqtable\(dq);

\f[I]// Delete second row\f[R]
table.deleteRow(1);
.EE
.SS Result
